%========   DVS ================

% ID   MOD   IDSUBDV   Value

% --- ID
%  id of the  DV
% --- MOD
% Could be SING / MULT   
% --- IDSUBDV
% If MOD is SING, it si the ID of the subdv. If MOD=MULTI, then is the ID of the group of subdvs


$INIDV
1    SING  1     589500000000.0
2    SING  2     0.31279
3    SING  3     2700.0
4    SING  4     0.25425
5    SING  5     0.16644
6    SING  6     0.07543
7    SING  7     0.03895
8    SING  8     0.01596
$ENDDV

%========   SUBDVS ================
%
%  ID   TAG IDTAG   SUBTAG
%
% ID
% id of the subdv
% TAG 
% is the category of the DV. Could be PROP / MAT / GRID / EXTFORCE 
% IDTAG
% is the ID specific entity to which  the subdv refers
% subTAG  
% is the category of the subDV. Available options depend on the TAG

$INISUBDV
1    MAT   1    YOUNG
2    MAT   1    POISSON
3    MAT   1    RHO
4    PROP  1    A
5    PROP  25   A
6    PROP  50   A
7    PROP  75   A
8    PROP  100  A
$ENDSUBDV



%========  SUBRESP  ================
% ID  TAG  IDTAG  SUBTAG 
%
% ID:
% ID of the subresponse
% TAG 
% is the category of the SUBRESP. Could be related to  STRESS / STRAIN / DISP / WEIGHT 
% IDTAG
% is the ID specific entity to which  the DV refers
% subTAG  
% Available options depend on the TAG

$INISUBRESP
1   DISP   108  MAGU                       
$ENDSUBRESP


%========  RESP

% ID   MOD   IDSUBRESP(if MOD is MULT)  AGGREGMODE  %EXTRA1 (if AGGREG is KS) 
%
% ID
% is the ID of the response
% MOD
% Could be SING or MULT.   If is SING it refers directly to only one subresponse. IF MULT, it refers to a group of Subresponses
% IDSUBRESP
% id of the subresponse (if MOD=SING) or group (if MOD=MULT)
% AGGREGMODE  (only for MOD= MULT)
% Is the way the group of subresponses are aggregated. Could be  SUM, L1, AVG,  L2, KS , KSadv
% EXTRA1   (only for MOD= MULT)
% Are double values to calibrate the KSadv method 


$INIRESP
1     SING      1
$ENDRESP
   

